(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the furnace operation" "proceed with furnace operation" "proceed with the kiln operation" "proceed with kiln operation" "authorize the furnace operation" "authorize furnace operation" "authorize the kiln operation" "authorize kiln operation" "finalize the furnace-operation decision" "finalize the furnace operation decision" "finalize the kiln-operation decision" "finalize the kiln operation decision" "declare the plant safety cleared" "declare plant safety cleared" "declare the plant floor safety cleared" "override the plant safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override plant safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799008181), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/glass-ceramics-plant-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-operator :no-plant :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-action)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "8181"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799008181: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8181 Glass and Ceramics Plant Operators plant scheduling/logistics-coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the ISCO-08 occupation-classification track (sibling to\nthe `cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8181\n-- Glass and Ceramics Plant Operators** only. This batch (Wave3)\ncontinues the 81xx plant-and-machine-operator range after Wave0/1/2\n(100% complete) and the entire 75xx craft-trades range (also\ncomplete), with 78 occupations already landed across batches 1-13\nbefore this ADR.\n\nA fresh `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8181` 404 check\nconfirmed no pre-existing repository before any work began -- a\ngenuinely fresh scaffold.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8181\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8181\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Glass and Ceramics Plant\nOperators\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR\nthe entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`.\n`kotoba.occupation.wave/wave-of` resolved this entry to wave 3, and\n`kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` read `{:total 436, :spec 119,\n:blueprint 0, :implemented 317}` at that same moment, matching the\nlive-truth baseline this batch was reset to immediately before work\nbegan. This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the `8181`\nentry to `:implemented`.\n\n**High-temperature furnace/kiln safety dimension.** Glass and Ceramics\nPlant Operators run high-temperature glass-melting furnaces and\nceramics kilns -- severe burn-hazard risk plus heavy-machinery hazard\nfrom forming/handling equipment. This actor is deliberately scoped to\n**plant scheduling/logistics coordination ONLY -- it never operates\nfurnace/kiln equipment, and it never finalizes a\nplant-operation-execution decision or a plant-safety-clearance\ndecision, and it never overrides a plant safety officer's judgment**.\nThose actions are a hard, permanent block in the governor, independent\nof confidence and independent of which op was proposed -- never\nauto-commit-eligible, never merely gated behind human escalation. The\nclosed op allowlist itself never includes any op that directly\nfinalizes a plant-operation-execution decision or a\nplant-safety-clearance decision, or overrides a plant safety officer's\njudgment; on top of that, an independent content-based scope-exclusion\ncheck on the proposal's free-text fields hard-blocks any attempt to\nsmuggle such a decision through an otherwise-allowlisted op. This\nmirrors the same class of guardrail this fleet has already applied to\nother domains with an irreversible physical/safety stake -- the\nreference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8114`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8114)\n(Cement, Stone and Other Mineral Products Machine Operators: a closely\nrelated heat-exposure industrial-plant-safety pattern -- `store`/\n`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full\ndoc set -- CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, LICENSE\n(AGPL-3.0-or-later), README.md, SECURITY.md, docs/business-model.md,\ndocs/operator-guide.md), freshly cloned and read in full in this\nsession (`deps.edn` coordinates for `io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`\ncopied verbatim, same `:git/sha` pin).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8181` as an OSS plant\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for independent glass and\nceramics plant-operator crews, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Glass and Ceramics Plant Coordination Advisor ⊣\nGlassCeramicsPlantCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger. `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` is deliberately NOT a `deps.edn` dependency of this actor\nrepo -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry depends on\nit.\n\nThis actor is **plant scheduling/logistics coordination ONLY, never\nplant-operation-execution or plant-safety-clearance authority** -- it\nmust NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose\nexercising any decision that directly finalizes a\nplant-operation-execution decision or a plant-safety-clearance\ndecision, or overrides a plant safety officer's judgment.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- production-run/inventory/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a burn-hazard/furnace-condition/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- raw-material/refractory-materials\n  procurement proposal\n\n`glassceramics.governor/allowed-ops` is a closed four-op `#{}` set --\nany `:op` outside it is unconditionally rejected as `:unknown-op`\n(`glassceramics.governor-test/hard-on-op-outside-closed-allowlist`,\nexercised end-to-end through the actor graph), and the mock advisor\n(`glassceramics.advisor/mock-advisor`) can only ever emit whatever `:op`\nthe request itself carried (its `infer` function merges the request\nthrough unchanged, with no path to synthesize a foreign op).\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (`glassceramics.governor/hard-violations`, permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **No operator** -- the crew member (`operator-record`) must be\n   independently verified/registered before any action; an\n   unregistered operator is a HARD block (`:no-operator`).\n2. **No plant** -- the plant site (`plant-record`) must be\n   independently verified/registered before any action; an\n   unregistered plant is a HARD block (`:no-plant`).\n3. **No actuation** -- `:effect` must be `:propose`; any other value\n   is a HARD block (`:no-actuation`) -- the governor never dispatches\n   hardware itself and never operates furnace/kiln equipment itself.\n4. **Unknown op** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op allowlist is\n   a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n5. **Scope-excluded action** -- independent of the op-allowlist check,\n   any proposal whose `:op` names, or whose `:rationale` text contains,\n   a plant-operation-execution finalization action (glass-melting\n   furnace or ceramics kiln cycle), a plant-safety-clearance\n   finalization action, or a plant-safety-officer-judgment override\n   action (`glassceramics.governor/scope-excluded-ops` and\n   `glassceramics.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`: \"proceed with the\n   furnace operation\", \"authorize the kiln operation\", \"finalize the\n   furnace-operation decision\", \"declare the plant safety cleared\",\n   \"override the plant safety officer's judgment\", and their variants)\n   is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally regardless of confidence. Full finalization/\n   execution ACTION phrases only, deliberately never bare nouns such\n   as \"glass\", \"ceramics\", \"kiln\" or \"furnace\" -- see the self-trip\n   guard section below.\n\n### One always-escalate op, one cost-threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence. Burn-hazard, furnace-condition and equipment-condition\n  concerns are never auto-resolved.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `glassceramics.governor/supply-cost-threshold` (2000) always needs\n  human sign-off, independent of confidence (inclusive boundary\n  verified by `glassceramics.governor-test/ok-supply-order-at-threshold-\n  boundary` -- exactly-at-threshold auto-commits, above-threshold\n  escalates per `glassceramics.governor-test/always-escalates-supply-\n  order-above-threshold`). This is deliberately an ESCALATE, not a HARD\n  block -- a cost overrun is a business decision a human can approve,\n  unlike the plant-operation/safety-clearance scope exclusion which is\n  permanently blocked.\n- advisor confidence below `glassceramics.governor/confidence-floor`\n  (0.6) also escalates, for any op\n  (`glassceramics.governor-test/escalates-low-confidence`).\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"glass\", \"kiln\", \"furnace\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- exactly the risk this\nvertical's own vocabulary (every routine work-log/schedule/safety-flag\nproposal necessarily mentions words like \"glass\", \"kiln\" or \"furnace\"\nin ordinary production/hazard-reporting context) could trigger if\nphrased carelessly. `glassceramics.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is\nphrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\nnouns, and `glassceramics.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-\nnever-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test\nasserting every op in the closed allowlist, driven through the default\nmock advisor (`glassceramics.advisor/mock-advisor`) with realistic\nfield values including a `:hazard-type :burn-hazard` field and a\n\"routine glass and ceramics production-run task\" task string, never\ntrips `:scope-excluded-action`. Green on this session's test run -- the\nguard was never observed to self-trip during verification.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8181\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to the\n  real repository (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-\n  isco-8181` / `cloud-itonami-isco-8181`), and `maturity-summary`'s\n  implemented count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the\n  registry via `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before\n  the edit, not assumed, to account for concurrent sibling agents\n  landing changes to the same registry file in this batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`) run against the actual pushed,\n  freshly re-cloned repository: 24 tests, 52 assertions, 0 failures, 0\n  errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/raw-output` and in\n  the task report.\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to this actor's own\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  depends on it.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-furnace-cycle` or\n  `:finalize-safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind\n  `always-escalate-ops` rather than structurally excluded: rejected\n  outright per the task's explicit guidance and this fleet's\n  established precedent for irreversible-safety-stake decisions -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  plant-operation-execution or plant-safety-clearance decision exists\n  in the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. This actor\n  coordinates plant scheduling/logistics only; the capability to\n  finalize plant operation or plant safety clearance, or to override a\n  plant safety officer's judgment, must not exist at all, hence a hard,\n  permanent, content-based block rather than an escalation gate.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. [\"glass\" \"kiln\"\n  \"furnace\"]): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above -- this actor's own domain necessarily mentions\n  \"glass\", \"kiln\" and \"furnace\" in ordinary work-log/schedule/\n  safety-flag rationale text, so a bare-noun list would risk\n  self-blocking the actor's own legitimate proposals. Phrased instead\n  as full finalization/execution action phrases, with a dedicated\n  regression test proving the default advisor's own proposals never\n  self-trip.\n- A numeric confidence-only gate for `:log-work-record`/\n  `:schedule-crew-operation`/`:coordinate-supply-order` (no\n  operator-provenance/plant-provenance or plant-operation/\n  safety-clearance content checks): rejected as insufficient --\n  confidence measures the advisor's certainty about the proposal it\n  chose to make, not whether that proposal cites an unregistered\n  operator/plant or smuggles a plant-operation/safety-clearance\n  finalization decision in its free text, which is exactly why the\n  operator/plant-provenance and scope-exclusion checks exist as\n  independent, content-based, permanent HARD blocks regardless of\n  confidence.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered operator AND an\n   independently registered plant (HARD-blocked otherwise by checks\n   1/2). Not a plant-operation or plant-safety-clearance decision in\n   any respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/shift/task *scheduling*\n   proposal (administrative logistics, e.g. \"assign operator to the\n   08:00-16:00 shift on the kiln line\"), never a\n   plant-operation-execution decision. Any free text that names a\n   plant-operation-execution finalization action, a\n   plant-safety-clearance finalization action, or a\n   plant-safety-officer-judgment override is independently HARD-blocked\n   by check 5 regardless of what op was used to carry it.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a burn-hazard/furnace-\n   condition/equipment-condition concern to a human; ALWAYS escalates,\n   unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER auto-commit\n   eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which the robot may\n   surface a safety observation, and it explicitly never resolves,\n   decides, or acts on anything itself.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- raw-material/refractory-materials\n   procurement proposal. Requires an independently registered operator\n   and plant (HARD-blocked otherwise by checks 1/2), and any proposal\n   above the registered cost threshold always escalates to a human,\n   independent of confidence. Not a plant-operation or\n   plant-safety-clearance action -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, directly\nfinalizes a plant-operation-execution decision or a\nplant-safety-clearance decision, or overrides a plant safety officer's\njudgment -- confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`glassceramics.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) the content-based,\nphrase-driven scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op` field\n(`glassceramics.governor/hard-violations`,\n`glassceramics.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`glassceramics.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`), tested directly\nagainst `governor/check`\n(`glassceramics.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-\nfurnace-operation-decision`,\n`glassceramics.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-kiln-\noperation-decision`,\n`glassceramics.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-plant-\nsafety-cleared`,\n`glassceramics.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-plant-\nsafety-officer-judgment`, and the rationale-content variants), and (c)\nthe dedicated self-trip regression proving the default mock advisor's\nown proposals, across all four allowlisted ops, never accidentally trip\nthat same block\n(`glassceramics.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip-on-scope-exclusion`)."), (:test/raw-output "Running tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting glassceramics.actor-test\n\nTesting glassceramics.governor-test\n\nRan 24 tests containing 52 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order supply-cost-threshold}"), (:test/counts "{:total 24, :assertions 52, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Glass and Ceramics Plant Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :operator-provenance :plant-provenance :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :plant-operation-safety-clearance-block)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8181"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8181"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8181)), (:test/simulator :glassceramics.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8181 — Glass and Ceramics Plant Operators Plant Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8181)))
